B.Nc=s(["The hammer landed first","The feather floated away"],t.s)
B.BG=new A.a2("fall-apollo","In 1971 an astronaut dropped a hammer and a feather on the Moon. What happened?","They landed at the same time",B.Nc,"The Moon has no air, so nothing held the feather back.",1,"\ud83d\udd28\ud83e\udeb6|The Moon, 1971")
B.Pu=s(["It stays the same","It gets slower and slower"],t.s)
B.BT=new A.a2("fall-faster-longer","A ball keeps falling. What happens to its speed?","It gets faster and faster",B.Pu,"Gravity keeps pulling, so a falling ball speeds up the longer it falls.",1,"\u26bd|Falling")
B.N2=s(["Gravity turns off","The skydiver gets lighter"],t.s)
B.Cu=new A.a2("fall-parachute","A skydiver opens a parachute and slows down. Why?","The big parachute catches a lot of air",B.N2,"Air pushes up on the wide parachute and balances the pull of gravity.",1,"\ud83e\ude82|Parachute")
B.P5=s(["The heavier ball","The lighter ball"],t.s)
B.CC=new A.a2("fall-tube","Two balls, one twice as heavy as the other, fall in a tall tube with all the air pumped out. Which lands first?","They land together",B.P5,"With no air, every object falls with the same speed-up, heavy or not.",2,"\ud83d\udd35\u26ab|No air")
B.NJ=s(["Gravity does not pull on marbles","The marble is secretly heavier"],t.s)
B.C4=new A.a2("fall-cancel","Earth pulls harder on a bowling ball than on a marble. So why do they fall together with no air?","The heavy ball is also harder to speed up, so it cancels out",B.NJ,"More pull and more stuff to move cancel out, so every object speeds up the same.",2,"\ud83c\udfb3\ud83d\udd2e|Heavy and light")
